// src/v4/test/claim/impossible_bug/suboptimal_complexity.dag
//
// Scope: TestClaim — suboptimal-complexity contract violation impossible-bug
//        class (R1). There is NO `complexity ≤ O(...)` annotation: complexity
//        IS coercion-cost (THESIS:187 unification), DERIVED by
//        lens/complexity.dag from Node structure. An operation whose
//        structural context bounds its cost (the bound its consuming
//        position / algebra inhabitance permits) but whose lens-derived
//        complexity exceeds that bound MUST error at compile time, not
//        review time. Bound = structural requirement; cost = lens-derived;
//        neither is a tag (feedback_no_annotations — compositional only).
// Anchor: THESIS.md "Enumerable impossible-bug classes" §374-376 R1 — the
//         CLASS only; THESIS's "annotated complexity ≤ O(n log n)" wording
//         is annotation shorthand, the modeled mechanism is a structural
//         cost bound + lens derivation. Also lens/complexity.dag.
//
// Owns:
//   - test_overcost_against_structural_bound_violates: TestClaim
//     - input: an operation at a position whose structural cost bound is
//       ≤ O(n log n) (propagated from its consumer / algebra inhabitance)
//       whose body lens/complexity.dag derives as O(n²)
//     - expected: Diagnostic { reason: SuboptimalComplexityViolation,
//       correction: Correction, at: <cost-violating composition> }
//   - test_within_structural_bound_passes: TestClaim
//     - input: the same body where no consuming position imposes a tighter
//       bound → compiles (the requirement is structural context, not a tag)
//   - test_cost_contradicts_inhabitance_caught: TestClaim
//     - input: an operation whose lens-derived cost contradicts the cost
//       class its algebra inhabitance fixes (e.g. a "constant-cost" monoid
//       op that composes a linear scan) → Diagnostic
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/verification.dag, std/diagnostic.dag, std/algebra.dag, lens/complexity.dag
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-14
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md.

module v4.test.claim.impossible_bug.suboptimal_complexity

